/-!
# Open-immersion Picard excision on locally factorial schemes

Let `X` be a Noetherian integral scheme whose local rings are unique factorization domains (for
instance a regular Noetherian integral scheme of dimension at most two), and let `j : U ⟶ X` be an
open immersion. Using the Weil–Cartier–Picard equivalence from
`TauCeti.AlgebraicGeometry.CartierDivisor.Factorial`, this file proves the open-immersion excision
exactness properties for `LineBundleClass.pullback j : Pic(X) → Pic(U)`:

* `TauCeti.AlgebraicGeometry.LineBundleClass.primeDivisorClass`: the line-bundle class
  `[𝒪_X(closure {η})] = [ℐ_{closure {η}}]⁻¹` of a codimension-one point `η` of `X`.
* `TauCeti.AlgebraicGeometry.LineBundleClass.pullback_surjective_of_isOpenImmersion`: restriction
  `Pic(X) → Pic(U)` is surjective.
* `TauCeti.AlgebraicGeometry.LineBundleClass.pullback_eq_one_iff_mem_closure_of_isOpenImmersion`
  and
  `TauCeti.AlgebraicGeometry.LineBundleClass.pullback_eq_one_iff_exists_prod_of_isOpenImmersion`:
  the kernel of `Pic(X) → Pic(U)` is generated by the classes `[𝒪_X(closure {η})]` of
  codimension-one points `η ∉ Set.range j` (and is spanned by a finite tuple when that complement
  is finite, with regular-surface specializations in dimension at most two).

## References

* R. Hartshorne, *Algebraic Geometry*, Chapter II, Proposition 6.5(c).
* [The Stacks Project, Tag 0BE9](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BE9) (Lemma 31.28.7) and
  [Tag 02RX](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02RX) (Lemma 42.19.3).
-/

public section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory Order TopologicalSpace

